title: "D3L Tool of NASA Satellite: a bilingual GUI for searching and downloading NASA MODIS/VIIRS/MERRA-2 data"
authors:
  - family-names: Dai
    given-names: Shaoqing
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0858-4728"
    email: dsq1993qingge@163.com
version: 2.1.1
date-released: "2026-10-22"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/GISerDaiShaoqing/D3LTool"
url: "https://gisersqdai.top/D3LTool/"
abstract: >-
  D3L Tool of NASA Satellite is a free, open-source desktop application
  for searching and downloading NASA Earth science data (MODIS, VIIRS from
  the LAADS DAAC, and MERRA-2 from the GES DISC). Built on NASA's official
  earthaccess library and the Common Metadata Repository (CMR) search
  service, it integrates authentication, product discovery (by product,
  date range, sinusoidal tile map, or bounding box), and a robust,
  resumable multi-threaded download queue in a bilingual (Chinese/English)
  PySide6 graphical interface, with a command-line interface sharing the
  same core library. Since v2.1 its capabilities are also exposed as
  Model Context Protocol (MCP) tools for AI clients and as a built-in
  conversational agent page, enabling natural-language data retrieval and
  download. It is designed for remote-sensing practitioners who do not
  write code and for users in network-constrained environments.
keywords:
  - NASA
  - MODIS
  - VIIRS
  - MERRA-2
  - remote sensing
  - Earthdata
  - LAADS
  - data download
  - MCP
  - AI agent
